            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Capture from the menu bar

Right-click Cubby's menu bar icon and the three capture actions are right
there: **Take Screenshot**, **Record Screen**, and **Copy Text from Screen**.
Click one and it starts, exactly as the keyboard gesture does.

Each one shows its gesture beside it, so the menu is also the place to look
when you have forgotten which keys do what — no more opening Settings to
check. If you have changed a shortcut, the menu shows *your* shortcut, not the
default.

This matters most if you would rather trigger Cubby with a mouse. In Settings,
under Shortcuts, set **Take a screenshot** to an ordinary key combination, then
bind your mouse's side button to that combination in its own software
(Logitech Options, Steermouse, and the like). Recording and text capture do
not have key combinations of their own — they are built on the screenshot
tap — so the menu is how you reach them once you have made that change. It is
now the only way, and that is exactly why it exists.
]]></description>
